{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle","id":1474513,"title":"Brainstorming how SL's could assassinate an athro GW ahroun ally mid-battle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-12T13:19:31-08:00","id":1474513,"title":"Brainstorming how SL's could assassinate an athro GW ahroun ally mid-battle","content":"In short:<br /> <br /> There are 6 weeks till a huge BSD battle, wherein the new GW athro Grand Elder will lure the BSD's into the caern, retreat, then return with an overwhelming number of allies to crush the BSD's before they can corrupt the caern.<br /> <br /> The former GE, a SL adren ahroun called Erases the Foe, is planning to use that chaos to remove the GW athro so that he can return to his position of power. He has 6 weeks to come up with a plan, along with the aid of his adren theurge SL packmate, and possibly a SL elder theurge from another sept who is sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Could you guys help me brainstorm ways that sufficiently motivated SL's could try and get away with this nefarious deed? 6 weeks is plenty of time to enact some serious plans, but I've never played high level games, and am at a bit of a loss as to what they might do. Find a way to isolate the GW athro and then summon an incarna of Grandfather Thunder? Find a way to ensure the athro is overrun by the BSD's?<br /> <br /> Any suggestions are most welcome.<br /> <br /> (Note: 1/2 the PC pack is firmly allied with the SL's, the other 1/2 reluctantly allied with the GW. I'm foreseeing a chance for excellent rp if they have to decide in the heat of the battle which faction to support.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T15:21:42-08:00","id":1474523,"title":"","content":"I think there are too many factors to have a true plan as too many things can go wrong in six weeks. Simple plans are the best, not elaborate ones, especially in combat. But in general, getting rid of rivals in battle like this fall into two typical categories.<br /> <br /> The first is the tactical retreat from battle at the moment when the target is at his most vulnerable and needs his &quot;allies&quot; to enter the fray. This allows the enemy to overwhelm the target and hopefully kill him. This is probably the safest option... unless the target (and possibly others) somehow manages to survive and tell everyone he was abandoned. But depending on circumstances, it might be too late for the target to save his crown since he's now seen as a loser or might not be believed. In any case, the betrayer needs to have a good story that fits most of what happened (why he left the battle).<br /> <br /> The second is to get a patsy... I mean assassin, who will kill the person at the right time in battle, hopefully in a way that hides it was an assassination because of the confusion in battle. Or perhaps before the battle when the target is alone, and then put the blame on the enemy for somehow sneaking into camp. This is much harder to pull off, but if the right time is found, it's more likely for the target to be killed - provided it can be done very quickly. (This would be a terrible option to do to a PC because most players will think it unfair, but is possible with an NPC).<br /> <br /> I think either could work for your purposes, it's just what fits in best with your plans. One thing you may want to do as an ST is to keep both options open, and then use whichever one works best for the scene as it plays out.<br /> <br /> There are lots of things you could do provided you're open to it. For example, maybe the SL adren ahroun knows a vampire who has Dominate. He makes a deal with that vampire. He arranges a trusted ally of the GW athro to meet with him, but it turns out the vampire is there and puts him into trance and implants a trigger that goes off in middle of battle (I don't think this technically can happen with the Dominate rules as written, but it is the type of thing Dominate is supposed to emulate). Or if you want a different flavor text, maybe the SL adren prays to Hakaken for aid, and the corrupt totem somehow aids him in exchange for some other service or ongoing worship. Then the packs of BSDs - subtly or directly influenced by Hakaken - make killing the GW athro the priority instead of things they would normally do to control the caern. ...because they know Hakaken will end up corrupting the SL adren and they'll eventually get control of the caern anyway. Or maybe get a bane to possess an ally (not turn him into fomori, just possess and use his body) and do the deed. But whatever it is, it deflects attention away from the SL adren ahroun as it is someone else who does the deed and clearly has no connection to the SL. More prosaically, you find an ally of the GW who is ambitious or greedy, and you pay him off some kind of bribe. Or maybe they offer lots of chiminage to a Pain spirit to wrack the GW athro at the right moment, crippling him in combat at precisely the worst moment so that he'll quickly fall in battle?<br /> <br /> What you prefer is going to be a matter of taste, and what makes sense within your chronicle.<br /> <br /> There are obviously other scenarios. The Shadow Lord faction might wait until after the battle is won, and then challenge the GW athro since he &quot;foolishly&quot; &quot;lost&quot; the caern originally, and attempt to kill him in a klaive duel. Or descend into a coup/civil war after all the allied Garou leave to go home (except for the SL elder theurge and other allies). This is more of a straight up civil war than betrayal.<br /> <br /> What gives you the kind of resolution, or choice for the PCs, that you want? Do you want the SL adren to be seen as more honorable? Less honorable, but still loyal to Gaia? Ambitious to the point he will make deals with enemies - vampires, Hakaken cultists, banes, etc.? Do you simply want to force the PCs to take sides? Have an ongoing mystery for them to investigate afterwards? Allow them the opportunity to see something &quot;wrong&quot; with an ally of the GW before or during battle (or that their new Grand Elder has been abandoned) and have a chance to intervene heroically (or choose to let him die)? Something else?<br /> <br /> I think once you know what kind of thing you want for the PCs, you'll be able to brainstorm something that puts them into that situation. And certain ideas might allow for multiple instances where the PCs might impact things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T10:08:15-08:00","id":1474571,"title":"","content":"Excellent post as always. Lots to think on/chew on. Here's a bit more information on what I'm hoping to achieve:<br /> <br /> Due to lots of great RP beforehand, the pack is split in their support of the ex-Grand Elder and the new one. They've all agreed to follow the new GE, but two members are close allies of the SL's and willing to help them return to power so as to back their long term vision for the Sept. As such, I want this betrayal moment to involve them and be a crucible for their loyalties both to the competing two factions and to their own pack.<br /> <br /> The SL adren was raised a Silver Fang but went SL at his Rite of Passage, and as such still shows elements of his nobility and integrity - but his deed name is Erases the Foe, and I want him to show why at this critical point. I want him to reveal his plan to the two PC's that support him at the critical moment during the fight, and force a crisis in the pack as they suddenly have to pick a side. (This desire for a crisis within the pack plays into visions they've had of their fate, and comes on the heels of many other RP-driven decisions they've made. Explaining it further is beyond the scope of this post.)<br /> <br /> The SL however would only remain a viable option for his two supporters if he doesn't go full Sith Lord on them; any plan on his part to use fomori, vampires, or other agents of the Wyrm would lose the PC's support and make it an easy choice for them.<br /> <br /> As such, I'm hoping to devise a plan that's clearly dark and twisted (killing a GE for supposed long term gain) but which doesn't use the Wyrm if possible. Hence why I was wondering about summoning an incarna of Grandfather Thunder, or... yeah. Not sure. Further complicating this is the fact that the GW athro ahroun is infamous for surviving impossible fights at the cost of her allies, and thus it would be very 'IC' for her to survive being stranded against numerous foes or other deadly situations. It would need to be an overwhelming strike that even her incredible abilities couldn't withstand. <br /> <br /> Perhaps something like the elder SL Theurge crafting a fetish that the PC's deploy at a critical moment to cripple her or trap her in some way? Force her into a uniquely crafted pocket realm prison? Something that the PC's could help the SL's craft over the course of the 6 weeks without realizing what they're working on? (One of the PC's is a theurge apprentice to Erases the Foe's SL theurge adren packmate.) And then, since the SL adren wouldn't be trusted to get close, they ask the PC's to deploy it instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-13T10:52:18-08:00","id":1474574,"title":"","content":"There's still plenty of options for an SL that remains firmly in the Gaian camp. I personally would not summon an incarna of Thunder. It's kind of overkill, and I don't think Thunder would want to be used to do the dirty work of one of his servants. It inverts the relationship he wants which is to be the one who dominates others. Thunder would want his children to come up their own methods. Plus summoning any kind of Incarna can go quickly wrong.<br /> <br /> I would suggest making use of a Pain spirit, an epiphling or semi-epiphling. They are part of Grandfather's Thunder's brood, and Pain-spirits are the listed teachers of such Gifts as Whelp Body (level 4 Ragabash) and Open Wounds (level 4 Shadow Lord). So it's adequately Gaian. It's detailed in Axis Mundi (also in the Ratkin book). It has a special charm Agony, that doubles wound penalties. It can't materialize in the physical world, but you can use various flavor text to get around it. Maybe you need to have the target wear something that, unknown to him, allows the spirit to use its Charm across the Gauntlet on the person who has it. And use one of the PCs to convince the GW to wear it, like offering it as a good luck charm. Or create your own unique Pain jaggling that can do more, but keep the flavor text. Or the SL NPC must ask the PCs to do things to perform the chiminage such as finding material correspondence, inflicting pain on themselves, agreeing to perform some future service, or anything else you need so the PCs are critical to the scene.<br /> <br /> The plot is basically to maneuver the Pain spirit in battle to strike the GW at pitch battle so he falls in combat much quicker against the BSDs than they otherwise would. Of course, your battle may take place in the Penumbra as well, so it's possible the spirit can be spotted. But perhaps it can be disguised or hidden, or presented in a way to make it seem that the BSDs summoned it. Or that it was simply attracted to such a horrific battle to oversee the merciless killing by the two sides.<br /> <br /> Or the Pain spirit is fashioned into a unique talen which is then given to one or more of the PCs to use against the NPC when it is the right time, so they need to stick close to the GW and &quot;help&quot; him. Tha talen would then do whatever combination of the Agony charm and/or the aforementioned Gifts, whatever works for you.<br /> <br /> It gives something for the elder SL Theurge to do (summon the right Pain spirit and properly prepare the chiminage, or perform Rite of Binding beforehand). So instead of just being random, he is essential to the plan.<br /> <br /> Pain Spirits are suppose to exist in order to warn people of their own mortality - the lesson of bodily pain. By respecting Pain, a mortal learns his own limitations. They hate people who deny their own pain as such people ignore the wisdom the Pain spirits want to teach. A GW athro who somehow survives impossible costs and lets others die as a result, might be someone who is need of their &quot;education&quot;. If the GW has followed the lessons of pain, those other Garou would be alive. What a terrible waste due to this guy's arrogance. You can present the scene of chiminage to the Pain spirit in the aspect that this is balancing an offense to the spirit world, and therefore appropriate to Gaia. But it's still a nasty betrayal and a terrible way to die while being wracked in pain. You could really twist the proverbial knife into the PCs consciences by presenting the NPC's death agony in a way that shows how awful it is.<br /> <br /> This is how I would approach the scene right now since it seems to hit the major points you want. But you and others can probably come up with lots of great ideas on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T08:39:03-08:00","id":1474627,"title":"","content":"Your pain jaggling idea is absolutely perfect, especially when combined with the rationale of the athro GW having ignored its lessons and the losses the nation has suffered as a result. Thank you! I'm going to take this idea and run with it. Maybe even have the PC's acquire material components from sites of great suffering over the course of the next 6 weeks, so that they're subtly involved in its creation without knowing what it'll truly be used for. Lots to work with here, it's still technically a Gaian ploy, and I think it'll really put the players in the right spot when the SL's reveal what the talen is and how they want the PC's to deploy it in the heat of battle.<br /> <br /> Many thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T09:10:31-08:00","id":1474628,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s an athro and an adren? I\u2019ve read some W:tA stuff and never seen these words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T09:27:38-08:00","id":1474629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1474628#post1474628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What\u2019s an athro and an adren? I\u2019ve read some W:tA stuff and never seen these words.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the official names (in setting) for a Rank 4 and Rank 3 Garou. They are in the corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T10:03:54-08:00","id":1474633,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Idk that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T22:20:22-08:00","id":1474785,"title":"","content":"I just have one quibble. Who made a plan where the BSDs were allowed anywhere near the Caern? And why didn't everyone tell them it was a dumb plan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T12:39:26-08:00","id":1474863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1474785#post1474785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just have one quibble. Who made a plan where the BSDs were allowed anywhere near the Caern? And why didn't everyone tell them it was a dumb plan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe it stems from this topic:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen\"> Rite of the Shrouded Glen - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So this level 4 rite renders the interior of a bawn permanently invisible if 10 gnosis is spent upon the casting... but what exactly is the benefit? I can see how it could be useful to prevent scrying, but beyond that...? So, a couple of questions: What does invisible mean, exactly? If somebody scries, do they see nothingness, indicating something is hidden? A penumbral reflection of what the land would look like without the caern being there? Or...? Does the rite prevent people walking up to the bawn from seeing what lies inside? Is the Sept invisible to just creatures of the wyrm, or anybody </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In general, the plan is risky, and one might oppose the plan with the tenet, that one must not take any action, that causes a caern to be violate. On the other hand, desperate times call for desperate measures. If the sept leader can't hope to defend the caern with the garou at his disposal such a strategy might be warranted. Sure, the BSD might harm the Caern while they are controlling it, but if the plan works the BSD will be on the defensive very quickly. And, assumed, the BSD need time to wear down the caern spirit and cause permanent damage to the Cearn, the risk might be necessary to take. Also, certain preparations could be made to protect the Caern and Caern spirit, so the BSD have a harder time hurting them, during their occupation.<br /> <br /> For better or for worse, the Galliards will tell of that battle...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T01:08:31-08:00","id":1474890,"title":"","content":"Honestly OP<br /> I think the New Elder's plan is stupid and breaks the litany, A Spiral perhaps needs only a second of time to desacrate the caern, and If I were the old elder I'd use this issue to rally my support and oust the new leader politically. From there I'd manouver my oppenent into harms way using the authority granted to me or quietly have him killed. Only very personal reasons would cloud my judgement enough to allow spirals in. Most spirals are pretty dumb, but there's usually a few smart fellows among them and there might be a spy in the sept,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T10:42:26-08:00","id":1474913,"title":"","content":"The OP already discussed the issue of how long it may take the Spirals to desecrate a caern in the other post that Heinrich linked to. He's using a variation of the rules for corrupting a caern found in the second Werewolf Players Guide, and he is using that as the ST to determine what is an appropriate response. You can come to a different conclusion in running your own chronicles, but he has already thought about this issue and decided what's appropriate using all the details going on in his chronicle.<br /> <br /> Basically the situation is this. The PCs sept in Detroit is heavily outnumbered by a BSD hive in Detroit. They just don't have the numbers to survive an attack. They'll be wiped out whenever the BSDs decide to attack. Nor can they succeed by attacking the Dancers first for the same reason. Simply standing and fighting just gets all the sept's Garou killed and the sept falls anyway. So instead, they have worked out a plan ahead of time to rally Garou from additional septs who can compensate for the greater BSD numbers. They know how long the BSD's rite of desecration will take in his chronicle setting, and the arrival of reinforcements is suppose to occur within the time period where the caern will still be uncorrupted. Is it risky? Yes. But there's not an alternative because the sept just can't magically create an entire army of new Garou to occupy the sept waiting until the BSDs come. They have to work within the limits they are under in terms of numbers and resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-19T10:21:49-08:00","id":1474987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1474890#post1474890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[....]A Spiral perhaps needs only a second of time to desacrate the caern, [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> pointed out, in the other topic <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26645_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26645\" data-vbnamecard=\"26645\">pwtucker</a> decided that BSDs would need to do something that is based on the rules for corrupting caerns and that, by extension, there is no way a desecration can be done &quot;in a second&quot;.<br /> It is another question, what amount of Occultism, Rituals or Wyrm Lore traits would be needed to know this and what the common believe among the garou population is.<br /> If the majority doesn't have the necessary knowledge and subscribes to a believe that BSDs could in fact rapidly desecrate a Caern, the Septleader might have a hard time to rally support for his plan. If, like I said, the sept leader on the other hand is convincing and has plans to boost the defences of Caern and Caern spirit, the sept might see the appeal of a plan that allows them to force the BSDs on the defensive and allows them to fight the enemy on their home turf.<br /> <br /> In any case, even if a planned counter-attack is happening, there will be a certain level of chaos, so planning for circumstances to perform an assassination, is kind of hard. 'Curse of Corruption' and 'Under the Gun' might help a Shadow Lord to get rid of someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T01:11:15-08:00","id":1475021,"title":"","content":"So we're all on board that this SL is well on their way to becoming a BSD right? Putting their personal vendetta over the defense of a Caern is pretty much abandoning all pretence of following the Tenets and living down to every single Shadow Lord stereotype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26564-badfurryfanfic","name":"BadFurryFanFic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T01:22:38-08:00","id":1475023,"title":"","content":"Even if there's a hypothetical &quot;rite&quot; to &quot;properly&quot; defile a caern that takes 10 minutes, sanctity can be broken or threatened with small acts. It's take me a long time to dismantle your home or your church, but that doesn't mean you'd be ok with someone smearing blood and shit over the walls, defacing your idols and dumping a barrel of toxic waste. Your Caern might be able to recover from that, there are RL temples that've gone through as much, but the sanctity has certainly been violated and symbolically, that's a big fucking loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T02:17:21-08:00","id":1475026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1475021#post1475021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're all on board that this SL is well on their way to becoming a BSD right? Putting their personal vendetta over the defense of a Caern is pretty much abandoning all pretence of following the Tenets and living down to every single Shadow Lord stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, possibly. Becoming a BSD is tied to dancing the spiral and is a Rite, it doesn't happen by accident. But depending on the Edition, there are plenty of 'proper' garou with more than questionable morals, tactics and opinions. And with &quot;corruption&quot; being an optional rule, that is meant to be employed if the ST runs a Ronin chronicle, there is really no way clear line, what a acceptable and what is not, other than in-universe opinions of their garou peers (and to some extend the ST awarding renown, for renown is awarded even to deeds not publicly known and can be discerned by spirits).<br /> <br /> Sure, it the tactic is only chosen for a personal vendetta, that is unwise and dishonorous. But, if the tactic has merit, in expectancy to win, lives saved among the sept's garou and kinfolk and other tactical considerations, than it is just very risky.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T02:26:19-08:00","id":1475027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1475023#post1475023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there's a hypothetical &quot;rite&quot; to &quot;properly&quot; defile a caern that takes 10 minutes, sanctity can be broken or threatened with small acts. It's take me a long time to dismantle your home or your church, but that doesn't mean you'd be ok with someone smearing blood and shit over the walls, defacing your idols and dumping a barrel of toxic waste. Your Caern might be able to recover from that, there are RL temples that've gone through as much, but the sanctity has certainly been violated and symbolically, that's a big fucking loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But again, it comes to the preparations the sept garou make before they fake their retreat to then counter attack.<br /> If the caern heart is concealed by bound spirits and trickster spirits are tasked to sabotage the BSDs efforts to run a ritual, then there is some layer of protection.<br /> Removing and storing objects of importance, like decorations from the shrine of fallen heroes and most certainly the path stone will also make desecration of these places/objects harder.<br /> <br /> Again, it comes down to the level of loss the sept might be willing to take.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T06:10:47-08:00","id":1475100,"title":"","content":"None of my NPC's think this plan is ideal, and most of the Sept is seriously disturbed by it. The new GE, however, has stated that she's open to better, safer plans. Thus far nobody's come forth with anything viable. As such, she's willing to take the political hit and risk the caern being sullied in exchange for destroying the BSD's and purifying the caern after. Also, the caern totem is Owl, and the way I'm running it Owl's given its blessing for what it perceives to be an ambush that's in line with its own modus operandi.<br /> <br /> But yes, everybody's concerned, there's been a lot of debate about the litany, and the whole plan hinges on the PC's and other sept packs being able to convince foreign septs to back the play. In short, it's proving to be a great way to stir up discussion, provoke my PC's to debate their loyalties, and get them to visit other septs as envoys for a desperate plan. <br /> <br /> As for the former GE shadow lord, this is very dark stuff that he's planning. His deed name, however, is Erases the Foe; he's going to try and remove the current GE *after* her plan has begun to work, so as to kill a rival and inherit the salvaged sept from her, while also disavowing her plan and claiming he'd never have allowed the caern to have been sullied. Is there room for disaster? Yes. Is he opening himself up to further corruption? Quite possibly. But the PC's are going to be the fulcrum of his plan, in that he'll ask them to execute it, and that will, again, prove a catalyst for great RP under tremendous pressure.<br /> <br /> At least, I hope so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T06:38:42-08:00","id":1475102,"title":"","content":"Well, good luck.<br /> I'm looking forward to read how it turned out.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Besides going to other septs (who are regularly understaffed as is) there might be an option to call in wandering packs, especially those serving Wyvern. Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T17:08:52-08:00","id":1475160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1475021#post1475021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we're all on board that this SL is well on their way to becoming a BSD right?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a big difference between secret murder and becoming a Black Spiral Dancer. This SL is certainly engaged in a capital crime. If discovered, he'd likely be subjected to the Punishment Rite of the Hunt. Though if his actions lead to the caern not being recovered, he could conceivably be subjected to the Rite of Gaia's Vengeance. But we're not told anything that indicates this guy is foredoomed into joining the Dancers. In fact, the earlier discussion is that the ST doesn't want to set this NPC up for a corruption arc. If he's not discovered and gets away with it, he might even prove to be an effective leader though one of dubious morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadFurryFanFic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1475021#post1475021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting their personal vendetta over the defense of a Caern is pretty much abandoning all pretence of following the Tenets and living down to every single Shadow Lord stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's certainly living up the SL stereotype. But to be honest, I think it's good for some stories to have some characters that fulfill that stereotype. If all you have is the opposites of the original stereotypes - a noble Shadow Lord, an effective Silver Fang who leads his people well, a thoughtful and considerate Get of Fenris, etc. -you're still doing a stereotype, just a different one. Having the occasional Shadow Lord conspiracy to take power is a good thing in a chronicle, in my opinion. It just shouldn't be the only thing they do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T02:07:00-08:00","id":1475208,"title":"","content":"There is also the fact that sometimes you need to take a bad leader out for the sake of the Nation and sept. If the leader is clearly unfit to lead but has a lot of physical power, they might need to be handled subtly.<br /> <br /> Shadow Lords do what they do for Gaia, so no one else has to. This means assassination, pretending to be a BSD, making deals with Nephandi, etc. It is not honourable work, but it is needed.<br /> <br /> And, of course, sometimes they think they can do a better job and so take out potential good leaders. High risk, high reward and all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T02:20:35-08:00","id":1475211,"title":"","content":"And, they aren't all-knowing, can't see the future, are subject to be mislead themselves, so what they do also is flawed more often than once.<br /> <br /> So, yes, what they do might be needed sometimes, but sometimes it is not. And what they do, is what they believe is best for Gaia, and the tribe, in that order, but still...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-22T08:09:23-08:00","id":1475234,"title":"","content":"A little more nuance: <br /> <br /> The sept in question is part of a confederacy of septs arranged around the Great Lakes, all of whom have pledged to support each other at least once a year in the face of threats, gather cubs for rites of passage, and gather occasionally to dictate confederacy policy. Each sept gets one vote at these councils. <br /> <br /> The former SL GE's plan was to create a number of low-ranked septs under his patronage in Detroit so as to develop regional power by means of his increased number of votes. The PC's, being under Mammoth, saw this as a way to increase garou unity by bringing a variety of different tribes to Detroit and helping them all work together. In particular, the SL's tolerance of metis and willingness to welcome all packs as long as they subscribed to his vision appealed to the PC's.<br /> <br /> The new GW GE, however, just wants to create a massive, powerful, old school sept that wages war on the wyrm. The PC's were dismayed when she won, because they saw their vision sliding down the tubes. Thus they are covertly still supporting the SL, in the hopes of helping him regain power and reinstate his plan. <br /> <br /> However, they've no idea he's planning to assassinate the GW. My hope is to put them in a bind when the moment comes, as they must decide whether the ends justify the means and agree to the assassination or reject the means and by doing so abandon the vision as well. <br /> <br /> My hope, therefore, is that the SL comes across as a more complex, nuanced figure than a mere cold hearted bastard; that he appeal to the PC's philosophies and dreams even as he forces them to ask how far they're willing to go to achieve them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T10:36:17-08:00","id":1475739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle#post1474513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short:<br /> <br /> There are 6 weeks till a huge BSD battle, wherein the new GW athro Grand Elder will lure the BSD's into the caern, retreat, then return with an overwhelming number of allies to crush the BSD's before they can corrupt the caern.<br /> <br /> The former GE, a SL adren ahroun called Erases the Foe, is planning to use that chaos to remove the GW athro so that he can return to his position of power. He has 6 weeks to come up with a plan, along with the aid of his adren theurge SL packmate, and possibly a SL elder theurge from another sept who is sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Could you guys help me brainstorm ways that sufficiently motivated SL's could try and get away with this nefarious deed? 6 weeks is plenty of time to enact some serious plans, but I've never played high level games, and am at a bit of a loss as to what they might do. Find a way to isolate the GW athro and then summon an incarna of Grandfather Thunder? Find a way to ensure the athro is overrun by the BSD's?<br /> <br /> Any suggestions are most welcome.<br /> <br /> (Note: 1/2 the PC pack is firmly allied with the SL's, the other 1/2 reluctantly allied with the GW. I'm foreseeing a chance for excellent rp if they have to decide in the heat of the battle which faction to support.)</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all: allowing the BSD to set foot in the caern is a major Litany violation and most likely those allies will tear this GW apart for just thinking about it. Second: why six weeks? Does this SL conspire with BSD so he knows the time of attack or it's just some form of challenge for GW: stand your ground for 6 weeks and I let you live. And one more thing: you didn't mention this GW auspice so it's a little harder to give you advices. But during one of my games I run a similar situation between Gaillard SL and Ahroun SF, both PCs, both leaders of the packs (mixed tribes, it was some kind of experiment), both trying to win the leadership of the caern for themselves (the leader was dying). In the wake of BSD attack (location of their HQ has just been found so the sept was preparing the counterattack) SL improvised an inspirational speech (about 10 minutes of pure roleplaying, combining Churchil, Patton and football coach techniques) and when the rest of the sept was ready to follow him through hell he pointed out that traditionally it is Ahroun's duty to lead warparties and who would be better leader than Ahroun SF? And the rest agreed. Now the Fang knew it's a trap but couldn't avoid it not loosing the face. So he accepted the burden of the command, the rest of the sept started to follow him (including the SL pack, it was part of his plan) than he said that he will stay behind on a maybe less glorious but equally important post as one of the caern guardians (after his speech there were only a handful of Garou who couldn't go anyway, like Guardian or Ritemaster). And then about the half of the warparty said &quot;HOOOOOLLLLLLLDDDD, he's right&quot; and stayed behind. Still SF had to lead the expedition and of course lost. OK, it's risky (if the Fang was succesful the SL would lose the race for leadership) but still it was one of the best plans I've ever heard, not to mention that it allow the SL to get away with murder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 03-03-2022, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T09:30:05-08:00","id":1475780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1475160#post1475160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's certainly living up the SL stereotype. But to be honest, I think it's good for some stories to have some characters that fulfill that stereotype. If all you have is the opposites of the original stereotypes - a noble Shadow Lord, an effective Silver Fang who leads his people well, a thoughtful and considerate Get of Fenris, etc. -you're still doing a stereotype, just a different one. Having the occasional Shadow Lord conspiracy to take power is a good thing in a chronicle, in my opinion. It just shouldn't be the only thing they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>My friend (the one who played SL mentioned above) always said that SL are everybody's best friend. But friendship also means business. Santiago (from Cyberpunk 2020) said: &quot;you don't let your personal caca get in the way of business&quot;. I believe that for SL the truth lies just in the middle. SL aren't honourless, they are just effective. Think about SL as you would think about a dark knight","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T08:16:02-07:00","id":1480832,"title":"","content":"Just an update: we finally got to the climactic battle for the Sept, and it couldn't have gone better. The players spent time leading up to it forging alliances with other septs, there was lots of grumbling from NPC's about the battle plan and how perilously close it came to relinquishing the Sept, but in the end some 50 garou mustered to launch the counter attack.<br /> <br /> All the while, I'd been encouraging the PC's splitting loyalties to the current GW elder and the previous SL. Only one PC caught on, but his attempts to warn the others weren't heeded. Was fascinating to watch - the GW lead through a populist, emotion-based appeal, while the SL was all cold logic and long term planning. The players resonated with one or the other, and over the following sessions aligned themselves accordingly.<br /> <br /> While this was going on, the GW asked the PC's to forge an alliance with a contentious wendigo sept, which they accomplished through great RP. The SL's then asked the PC's to acquire a shattered klaive of great historical significance from the Wendigo, promising to try and forge a grand klaive for them as a sign of their investment in the alliance.<br /> <br /> Which made the moment when the SL's accosted the PC's mid-battle to retake the sept with the pain jaggling talen based on the klaive shards all the sweeter. They tasked the PC's with paralyzing the GW at a crucial moment, then left.<br /> <br /> The pack then imploded. <br /> <br /> One PC was so outraged at being manipulated, and so loyal to the GW that he simply ran off, refusing to talk about it. The alpha kept demanding the talen be handed over, but the two-SL aligned PC's refused, with the philodox asking over and over again that they try and find a solution.<br /> <br /> Tempers rose, and with time running out, they were forced to join the main battle without hitting on a solution.<br /> <br /> The philodox, who'd been the one who'd seen this coming, ended up using the talen at a pivotal moment, leading the GW's horrific death.<br /> <br /> The philodox left the pack, as his packmates all felt betrayed, their totem, Mammoth, left the pack, and the other SL-aligned pc was allowed to stay on a provisional member. The pack refused to stay in the sept after the SL retook the GE position, and left for Chicago, where we're about to start a new arc.<br /> <br /> Fantastic RP. The players loved it. Super intense, high emotions, huge consequences to their actions. Thanks so much to everyone who helped this come about with their advice - it was worth its weight in gold!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-12T17:17:09-07:00","id":1480896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474513-brainstorming-how-sl-s-could-assassinate-an-athro-gw-ahroun-ally-mid-battle?p=1480832#post1480832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks so much to everyone who helped this come about with their advice - it was worth its weight in gold!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you liked it. It's a shame that this forum limits don't allow you to show us all that (maybe next time you should record that \ud83d\ude09). I like that idea of talen. And from what I see you have players who can overcome their friendship in favour of role playing. It's rare so good for you. Best wishes you all. Hope we'll hear some more of your endavours sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}